					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modern-erasmus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3129691); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3129691&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1610097697" alt="Modern_Erasmus" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3129691)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modern-erasmus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3129691); return false;" >Modern_Erasmus</a></span> <span class="odate time_1506111136 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Sep 2017 20:12</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3599646">
									

<p>Going to re-iterate from my prior critique that this just isn't how professionals interact, even on relatively casual work chats. In my NGO's slack for example, which is hardly a tower of professionalism, no one would be caught dead doing some of the stuff seen here. And we're supposed to buy that this is the ethics committee?</p>
<p>Honestly, the only way an irc chat ethics committee could work would be as a comedic parody. As is, it's so divorced from both irl standards for work chats and the simple subject matter at hand that the tone of the piece is just baffling. The bit about holding onto close friends is also somewhat alien to the logistics of working relationships.</p>
<p>I get what you're going for, I really do. Portray the ethics committee like how us authors act in 19. But that is just not how adult professionals interact, even in a casual chat. Anonymity and the fact that the vast majority of our chat members are in the 15-22 range makes our interactions trend towards meme humor and casual discourse. This would never be the case for any work chat, much less a subset of something like the ethics committee.</p>
<p>The frequent attempts to rationalize both their use of irc and non professional discourse also only draw more attention to the problems rather than offering a satisfying explanation.</p>

							</div>

								
