		<div class="post" id="post-3940738">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,3940738)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-3940738">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/skatetroe" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1957145); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1957145&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1610097697" alt="SkateTroe" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1957145)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/skatetroe" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1957145); return false;" >SkateTroe</a></span> <span class="odate time_1535551486 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Aug 2018 14:04</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3940738">
									

<p>I agree with you that it's a bit overly casual for a workspace, but I think the author could be setting up a really powerful juxtaposition, depending on how they write future parts (which I haven't checked if they're out yet).</p>
<p>Having this chill friendly air about the EC gives you a level to suddenly snap away from when the harsh realities of being an Observer come into play. Basically, this could be a powerful baseline to move on from depending on how they choose to handle things.</p>
<p>Also worth noting, the Ethics Committee are mired in the absolute worst of <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">humanity</span> existence as a whole. Maybe they in particular need somewhere that they can be that casual?</p>

							</div>

								
					
