																		New way to see things
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vermillion-fenrir" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1747245); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1747245&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1610097697" alt="Vermillion Fenrir" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1747245)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vermillion-fenrir" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1747245); return false;" >Vermillion Fenrir</a></span> <span class="odate time_1564274010 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Jul 2019 00:33</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4316399">
									

<p>From what I seen on the <strong><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/ethics-committee-orientation">Ethics Committee Orientation</a></strong>, I always see them as the lawbringer of the Foundation, the &quot;Lawful Good&quot; side that decides on what is acceptable and what is not, what is morally wrong and right. I see them as someone strict and stern, as those that decide how justice should be done.</p>
<p>Well&#8230; this&#8230;. flips that upside down&#8230;.</p>
<p>But on the contrary, I'm not upset. I actually love to see their casual side, portrayed in lighthearted and comical manner. Really bring a new perspective to the Ethics Committee.</p>
<p>Lovely tale, +1</p>

							</div>

								
					
